IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc22-trial.l4 -- sections 645 to 654 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46 (Part XX: trial; taking evidence; separation of jurors; presence of the accused; counsel of record; summing up; view; jury retiring; disagreement; mistrial). Part agent ccc22. Layer 1: the law, objectively.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- How a result reads: JUST TRUE (the text's own words bring the case within the rule); JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words); NOTHING (not covered). A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Tags in the comments: [M-a] a failed "if"/"where" or a flat negative counted as the text's no; [M-b] a prohibition or grant limited by its own wording counted as NOT the text's no (NOTHING);
-- [F:...] a fork line for NOTES.md (may-if, may-where, entitled, duty, unless). Section 2 terms and other parts' answers are INPUTS named for their section.

§ `Section 645 -- Trial continuous`

-- src:13031 | 645 (1) The trial of an accused shall proceed continuously subject to adjournment by the court.
@ref s 645(1) (src:13031-13031)
GIVEN `the court has adjourned the trial` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 645(1) the trial must proceed continuously` MEANS
    IF `the court has adjourned the trial`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall proceed continuously subject to adjournment by the court" [F:unless] [M-a]
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:13033 | (2) A judge may adjourn a trial from time to time in the same sittings.
@ref s 645(2) (src:13033-13033)
GIVEN `the adjournment is from time to time in the same sittings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 645(2) a judge may adjourn the trial` MEANS
    IF `the adjournment is from time to time in the same sittings`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A judge may adjourn a trial from time to time in the same sittings"

-- src:13035 | (3) For the purpose of subsection (2), no formal adjournment of trial or entry thereof is required.
@ref s 645(3) (src:13035-13035)
GIVEN `the adjournment is for the purpose of subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 645(3) a formal adjournment of the trial or an entry of it is required` MEANS
    IF `the adjournment is for the purpose of subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "For the purpose of subsection (2), no formal adjournment of trial or entry thereof is required" [M-a]
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purpose of subsection (2)"

-- src:13037 | (3.1) In deciding whether to adjourn the trial, the judge shall consider the interests of justice, including the interests of any victim of the offence in question if information related to the victim’s interests is readily available.
@ref s 645(3.1) (src:13037-13037)
GIVEN `the judge is deciding whether to adjourn the trial` IS A BOOLEAN
      `information related to the victim’s interests is readily available` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 645(3.1) the judge must consider the interests of any victim of the offence in question` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the judge is deciding whether to adjourn the trial` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In deciding whether to adjourn the trial"
        IF `information related to the victim’s interests is readily available` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "including the interests of any victim of the offence in question if information related to the victim’s interests is readily available" [M-a] [F:duty]

-- src:13039 | (4) A judge, in any case tried without a jury, may reserve final decision on any question raised at the trial, or any matter raised further to a pre-hearing conference, and the decision, when given, shall be deemed to have been given at the trial.
@ref s 645(4) (src:13039-13039)
GIVEN `the case is tried without a jury` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 645(4) a judge may reserve final decision on any question raised at the trial, or any matter raised further to a pre-hearing conference` MEANS
    IF `the case is tried without a jury`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A judge, in any case tried without a jury"

-- src:13039 | (4) A judge, in any case tried without a jury, may reserve final decision on any question raised at the trial, or any matter raised further to a pre-hearing conference, and the decision, when given, shall be deemed to have been given at the trial.
@ref s 645(4) (src:13039-13039)
GIVEN `the decision was reserved under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision has been given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 645(4) the decision is deemed to have been given at the trial` MEANS
    IF `the decision was reserved under subsection (4)` AND `the decision has been given`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the decision, when given, shall be deemed to have been given at the trial" (not yet given, or not reserved under this subsection) [M-a]

-- src:13041 | (5) In any case to be tried with a jury, the judge before whom an accused is or is to be tried has jurisdiction, before any juror on a panel of jurors is called pursuant to subsection 631(3) or (3.1) and in the absence of any such juror, to deal with any matter that would ordinarily or necessarily be dealt with in the absence of the jury after it has been sworn.
@ref s 645(5) (src:13041-13041)
GIVEN `the case is to be tried with a jury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no juror on a panel of jurors has yet been called pursuant to subsection 631(3) or (3.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is one that would ordinarily or necessarily be dealt with in the absence of the jury after it has been sworn` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 645(5) the judge has jurisdiction to deal with the matter` MEANS
    IF `the case is to be tried with a jury` AND `no juror on a panel of jurors has yet been called pursuant to subsection 631(3) or (3.1)` AND `the matter is one that would ordinarily or necessarily be dealt with in the absence of the jury after it has been sworn`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "has jurisdiction, before any juror on a panel of jurors is called pursuant to subsection 631(3) or (3.1) and in the absence of any such juror, to deal with any matter that would ordinarily or necessarily be dealt with in the absence of the jury"

-- src:13043 | 646 On the trial of an accused for an indictable offence, the evidence of the witnesses for the prosecutor and the accused and the addresses of the prosecutor and the accused or counsel for the accused by way of summing up shall be taken in accordance with the provisions of Part XVIII, other than subsections 540(7) to (9), relating to the taking of evidence at preliminary inquiries.
@ref s 646 (src:13043-13043)
GIVEN `the trial is for an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision is a provision of Part XVIII relating to the taking of evidence at preliminary inquiries` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision` IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 646 the provision of Part XVIII applies to the taking of the evidence and the addresses` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the trial is for an indictable offence` AND `the provision is a provision of Part XVIII relating to the taking of evidence at preliminary inquiries`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On the trial of an accused for an indictable offence ... in accordance with the provisions of Part XVIII ... relating to the taking of evidence at preliminary inquiries"
        IF `the provision`'s `section` EQUALS 540 AND (`the provision`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(7)" OR `the provision`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(8)" OR `the provision`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(9)") THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in accordance with the provisions of Part XVIII, other than subsections 540(7) to (9)" [F:duty] [M-a]
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Sections 647 to 648 -- Separation of jurors; restriction on publication`

-- src:13045 | 647 (1) The judge may, at any time before the jury retires to consider its verdict, permit the members of the jury to separate.
@ref s 647(1) (src:13045-13045)
GIVEN `the jury has retired to consider its verdict` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 647(1) the judge may permit the members of the jury to separate` MEANS
    IF `the jury has retired to consider its verdict`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at any time before the jury retires to consider its verdict" (a period the text fixes in its own words: ruling (a) of 2026-11-05) [F:may-where] [M-a]
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:13047 | (2) Where permission to separate under subsection (1) cannot be given or is not given, the jury shall be kept under the charge of an officer of the court as the judge directs, and that officer shall prevent the jurors from communicating with anyone other than himself or another member of the jury without leave of the judge.
@ref s 647(2) (src:13047-13047)
GIVEN `permission to separate under subsection (1) cannot be given or is not given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 647(2) the jury must be kept under the charge of an officer of the court as the judge directs` MEANS
    IF `permission to separate under subsection (1) cannot be given or is not given`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where permission to separate under subsection (1) cannot be given or is not given, the jury shall be kept under the charge of an officer of the court" [M-a] [F:duty]

-- src:13047 | (2) Where permission to separate under subsection (1) cannot be given or is not given, the jury shall be kept under the charge of an officer of the court as the judge directs, and that officer shall prevent the jurors from communicating with anyone other than himself or another member of the jury without leave of the judge.
@ref s 647(2) (src:13047-13047)
GIVEN `the juror would communicate with the officer or another member of the jury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge has given leave` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 647(2) the officer must prevent the juror from communicating` MEANS
    IF `the juror would communicate with the officer or another member of the jury` OR `the judge has given leave`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall prevent the jurors from communicating with anyone other than himself or another member of the jury without leave of the judge" [F:unless] [M-a]
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:13049 | (3) Failure to comply with subsection (2) does not affect the validity of the proceedings.
@ref s 647(3) (src:13049-13049)
GIVEN `the failure is a failure to comply with subsection 647(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 647(3) the failure to comply affects the validity of the proceedings` MEANS
    IF `the failure is a failure to comply with subsection 647(2)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Failure to comply with subsection (2) does not affect the validity of the proceedings" [M-a]
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Failure to comply with subsection (2)"

-- src:13051 | (4) Where the fact that there has been a failure to comply with this section or section 648 is discovered before the verdict of the jury is returned, the judge may, if he considers that the failure to comply might lead to a miscarriage of justice, discharge the jury and
-- src:13052 | (a) direct that the accused be tried with a new jury during the same session or sittings of the court; or
-- src:13053 | (b) postpone the trial on such terms as justice may require.
@ref s 647(4) (src:13051-13053)
DECLARE `s 647(4) the course the judge takes` IS ONE OF
    `s 647(4)(a) direct that the accused be tried with a new jury during the same session or sittings of the court`
    `s 647(4)(b) postpone the trial on such terms as justice may require`
    `s 647(4) some other course`

-- src:13051 | (4) Where the fact that there has been a failure to comply with this section or section 648 is discovered before the verdict of the jury is returned, the judge may, if he considers that the failure to comply might lead to a miscarriage of justice, discharge the jury and
-- src:13052 | (a) direct that the accused be tried with a new jury during the same session or sittings of the court; or
-- src:13053 | (b) postpone the trial on such terms as justice may require.
@ref s 647(4) (src:13051-13053)
GIVEN `the failure to comply with section 647 or 648 is discovered before the verdict of the jury is returned` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge considers that the failure to comply might lead to a miscarriage of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
      course IS A `s 647(4) the course the judge takes`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 647(4) the judge may discharge the jury and take the course` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the failure to comply with section 647 or 648 is discovered before the verdict of the jury is returned` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the fact that there has been a failure to comply with this section or section 648 is discovered before the verdict of the jury is returned, the judge may" [F:may-where] [M-a]
        IF NOT `the judge considers that the failure to comply might lead to a miscarriage of justice` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if he considers that the failure to comply might lead to a miscarriage of justice" [F:may-if]
        IF course EQUALS `s 647(4) some other course` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "discharge the jury and (a) direct that the accused be tried with a new jury during the same session or sittings of the court; or (b) postpone the trial"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:13055 | (5) The judge shall direct the sheriff to provide the jurors who are sworn with suitable and sufficient refreshment, food and lodging while they are together until they have given their verdict.
@ref s 647(5) (src:13055-13055)
GIVEN `the jurors are sworn` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the jurors are together` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the jurors have given their verdict` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 647(5) the judge must direct the sheriff to provide the jurors with suitable and sufficient refreshment, food and lodging` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the jurors are sworn` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the jurors who are sworn"
        IF `the jurors have given their verdict` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "while they are together until they have given their verdict" [M-a]
        IF `the jurors are together` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "while they are together" [M-a] [F:duty]

-- 648(1), the BAR: JUST TRUE where the information falls within the prohibition (after permission to separate is given and before the jury retires).
-- src:13057 | 648 (1) After permission to separate is given to members of a jury under subsection 647(1), no information regarding any portion of the trial at which the jury is not present shall be published in any document or broadcast or transmitted in any way before the jury retires to consider its verdict.
@ref s 648(1) (src:13057-13057)
GIVEN `permission to separate has been given to members of the jury under subsection 647(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information regards a portion of the trial at which the jury is not present` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the jury has retired to consider its verdict` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 648(1) the section bars publishing, broadcasting or transmitting the information` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the information regards a portion of the trial at which the jury is not present` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "no information regarding any portion of the trial at which the jury is not present"
        IF (NOT `permission to separate has been given to members of the jury under subsection 647(1)`) OR `the jury has retired to consider its verdict` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "After permission to separate is given to members of a jury under subsection 647(1) ... before the jury retires to consider its verdict" (outside the period) [M-a]
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:13059 | (2) Every one who fails to comply with subsection (1) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 648(2) (src:13059-13059)
GIVEN `the person fails to comply with subsection 648(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 648(2) the person is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction` MEANS
    IF `the person fails to comply with subsection 648(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every one who fails to comply with subsection (1)"

-- What the subsection states about gravity and penalty: the class of offence, and no maximum (the penalty for a summary conviction offence with none stated is in section 787, another part).
-- src:13059 | (2) Every one who fails to comply with subsection (1) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 648(2) (src:13059-13059)
GIVETH A `Punishment`
`s 648(2) the punishment the subsection states` MEANS
    Punishment WITH `mode` IS `on summary conviction`
                  , `maximum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`
                  , `minimum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`
                  , `maximum fine` IS `no fine is stated`
                  , `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`

-- src:13059 | (2) Every one who fails to comply with subsection (1) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 648(2) (src:13059-13059)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 648(2) the class of offence` MEANS `an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:13060 | (3) [Repealed, 2005, c. 32, s. 21]
@ref s 648(3) (repealed) (src:13060-13060)
`s 648(3) what the text shows` MEANS "[Repealed, 2005, c. 32, s. 21]"

§ `Section 649 -- Disclosure of jury proceedings`

-- src:13062 | 649 (1) Every member of a jury, and every person providing technical, personal, interpretative or other support services to a juror with a physical disability, who discloses any information relating to the proceedings of the jury when it was absent from the courtroom that was not subsequently disclosed in open court is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 649(1) (src:13062-13062)
GIVEN `the person is a member of a jury or a person providing technical, personal, interpretative or other support services to a juror with a physical disability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person discloses information relating to the proceedings of the jury when it was absent from the courtroom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information was subsequently disclosed in open court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 649(1) the person is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is a member of a jury or a person providing technical, personal, interpretative or other support services to a juror with a physical disability` AND `the person discloses information relating to the proceedings of the jury when it was absent from the courtroom`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every member of a jury, and every person providing technical, personal, interpretative or other support services to a juror with a physical disability, who discloses any information relating to the proceedings of the jury when it was absent from the courtroom"
        IF `the information was subsequently disclosed in open court` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "that was not subsequently disclosed in open court" [M-b]
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:13062 | 649 (1) Every member of a jury, and every person providing technical, personal, interpretative or other support services to a juror with a physical disability, who discloses any information relating to the proceedings of the jury when it was absent from the courtroom that was not subsequently disclosed in open court is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 649(1) (src:13062-13062)
DECLARE `s 649(1) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 649(1) disclose information relating to the proceedings of the jury when it was absent from the courtroom`

@ref s 649(1) (src:13062-13062)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 649(1) action`
`s 649(1) a juror shall not disclose information relating to the proceedings of the jury` MEANS
    PARTY `a juror`
    SHANT `s 649(1) disclose information relating to the proceedings of the jury when it was absent from the courtroom`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the juror disclosed information relating to the proceedings of the jury when it was absent from the courtroom"

-- src:13064 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply in respect of the disclosure of information for the purposes of
-- src:13065 | (a) an investigation of an alleged offence under subsection 139(2) in relation to a juror;
-- src:13066 | (b) giving evidence in criminal proceedings in relation to such an offence; or
-- src:13067 | (c) any medical or psychiatric treatment or any therapy or counselling that a person referred to in subsection (1) receives from a health care professional after the completion of the trial in relation to health issues arising out of or related to the person’s service at the trial as a juror or as a person who provided support services to a juror.
@ref s 649(2) (src:13064-13067)
DECLARE `s 649(2) the purpose of the disclosure` IS ONE OF
    `s 649(2)(a) an investigation of an alleged offence under subsection 139(2) in relation to a juror`
    `s 649(2)(b) giving evidence in criminal proceedings in relation to such an offence`
    `s 649(2)(c) any medical or psychiatric treatment or any therapy or counselling that the person receives from a health care professional after the completion of the trial in relation to health issues arising out of or related to the person’s service at the trial`
    `s 649(2) some other purpose`

-- src:13064 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply in respect of the disclosure of information for the purposes of
-- src:13065 | (a) an investigation of an alleged offence under subsection 139(2) in relation to a juror;
-- src:13066 | (b) giving evidence in criminal proceedings in relation to such an offence; or
-- src:13067 | (c) any medical or psychiatric treatment or any therapy or counselling that a person referred to in subsection (1) receives from a health care professional after the completion of the trial in relation to health issues arising out of or related to the person’s service at the trial as a juror or as a person who provided support services to a juror.
@ref s 649(2) (src:13064-13067)
GIVEN purpose IS A `s 649(2) the purpose of the disclosure`
      `the answer of s 649(3) for the health care professional` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 649(2) subsection (1) applies to the disclosure` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF purpose EQUALS `s 649(2)(a) an investigation of an alleged offence under subsection 139(2) in relation to a juror` OR purpose EQUALS `s 649(2)(b) giving evidence in criminal proceedings in relation to such an offence` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply in respect of the disclosure of information for the purposes of (a) an investigation of an alleged offence under subsection 139(2) in relation to a juror; (b) giving evidence in criminal proceedings in relation to such an offence" [M-a]
        IF purpose EQUALS `s 649(2)(c) any medical or psychiatric treatment or any therapy or counselling that the person receives from a health care professional after the completion of the trial in relation to health issues arising out of or related to the person’s service at the trial` AND `the answer of s 649(3) for the health care professional` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) any medical or psychiatric treatment or any therapy or counselling that a person referred to in subsection (1) receives from a health care professional after the completion of the trial" [M-a]
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsection (1) does not apply in respect of the disclosure of information for the purposes of" the three listed purposes (a purpose outside them, or a professional section 649(3) does not accept, is not decided here)

-- src:13069 | (3) For the purpose of paragraph (2)‍(c), the health care professional who provides any medical or psychiatric treatment or any therapy or counselling must be entitled to do so under the laws of a province.
@ref s 649(3) (src:13069-13069)
GIVEN `the health care professional is entitled to provide the treatment, therapy or counselling under the laws of a province` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 649(3) the health care professional is one for the purpose of paragraph (2)(c)` MEANS
    IF `the health care professional is entitled to provide the treatment, therapy or counselling under the laws of a province`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be entitled to do so under the laws of a province" [M-a]

§ `Section 650 -- Accused to be present`

-- src:13071 | 650 (1) Subject to subsections (1.1) and (2) and section 650.01, an accused, other than an organization, shall be present in court during the whole of their trial, either in person or, if authorized under any of sections 715.231 to 715.241, by audioconference or videoconference.
@ref s 650(1) (src:13071-13071)
GIVEN `s 2 organization: the accused is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 650(1) the section requires the accused to be present in court during the whole of their trial` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 2 organization: the accused is one`
    WHEN JUST isOrg THEN
        (IF isOrg
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an accused, other than an organization, shall be present in court" [F:duty] [M-a]
         ELSE JUST TRUE)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the accused is an organization is for s 2 "organization"

-- src:13071 | 650 (1) Subject to subsections (1.1) and (2) and section 650.01, an accused, other than an organization, shall be present in court during the whole of their trial, either in person or, if authorized under any of sections 715.231 to 715.241, by audioconference or videoconference.
@ref s 650(1) (src:13071-13071)
GIVEN `the accused is present in court in person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused appears by audioconference or videoconference authorized under any of sections 715.231 to 715.241` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 650(1) the accused’s presence meets the requirement` MEANS
    IF `the accused is present in court in person` OR `the accused appears by audioconference or videoconference authorized under any of sections 715.231 to 715.241`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be present in court during the whole of their trial, either in person or, if authorized under any of sections 715.231 to 715.241, by audioconference or videoconference" [M-a] [F:duty]

-- src:13073 | (1.1) The court may, with the consent of the prosecutor and the accused, allow the accused to appear by counsel for any part of the trial, other than a part in which the evidence of a witness is taken.
@ref s 650(1.1) (src:13073-13073)
GIVEN `the prosecutor consents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused consents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the part is a part in which the evidence of a witness is taken` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 650(1.1) the court may allow the accused to appear by counsel for the part of the trial` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the prosecutor consents` AND `the accused consents`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "with the consent of the prosecutor and the accused"
        IF `the part is a part in which the evidence of a witness is taken` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for any part of the trial, other than a part in which the evidence of a witness is taken" [F:unless] [M-a]
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:13074 | (1.2) [Repealed, 2022, c. 17, s. 39]
@ref s 650(1.2) (repealed) (src:13074-13074)
`s 650(1.2) what the text shows` MEANS "[Repealed, 2022, c. 17, s. 39]"

-- src:13076 | (2) The court may
-- src:13077 | (a) cause the accused to be removed and to be kept out of court, where he misconducts himself by interrupting the proceedings so that to continue the proceedings in his presence would not be feasible;
-- src:13078 | (b) permit the accused to be out of court during the whole or any part of his trial on such conditions as the court considers proper; or
-- src:13079 | (c) cause the accused to be removed and to be kept out of court during the trial of an issue as to whether the accused is unfit to stand trial, where it is satisfied that failure to do so might have an adverse effect on the mental condition of the accused.
@ref s 650(2) (src:13076-13079)
DECLARE `s 650(2) the course` IS ONE OF
    `s 650(2)(a) cause the accused to be removed and to be kept out of court, where they misconduct themself by interrupting the proceedings so that to continue the proceedings in their presence would not be feasible`
    `s 650(2)(b) permit the accused to be out of court during the whole or any part of the trial on such conditions as the court considers proper`
    `s 650(2)(c) cause the accused to be removed and to be kept out of court during the trial of an issue as to whether the accused is unfit to stand trial`
    `s 650(2) some other course`

-- src:13076 | (2) The court may
-- src:13077 | (a) cause the accused to be removed and to be kept out of court, where he misconducts himself by interrupting the proceedings so that to continue the proceedings in his presence would not be feasible;
-- src:13078 | (b) permit the accused to be out of court during the whole or any part of his trial on such conditions as the court considers proper; or
-- src:13079 | (c) cause the accused to be removed and to be kept out of court during the trial of an issue as to whether the accused is unfit to stand trial, where it is satisfied that failure to do so might have an adverse effect on the mental condition of the accused.
@ref s 650(2) (src:13076-13079)
GIVEN course IS A `s 650(2) the course`
      `the accused misconducts themself by interrupting the proceedings so that to continue the proceedings in their presence would not be feasible` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that failure to remove the accused during the trial of the issue of fitness might have an adverse effect on the mental condition of the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 650(2) the court may take the course` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF course EQUALS `s 650(2) some other course` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The court may (a) ...; (b) ...; or (c) ..."
        IF course EQUALS `s 650(2)(a) cause the accused to be removed and to be kept out of court, where they misconduct themself by interrupting the proceedings so that to continue the proceedings in their presence would not be feasible` AND (NOT `the accused misconducts themself by interrupting the proceedings so that to continue the proceedings in their presence would not be feasible`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where he misconducts himself by interrupting the proceedings so that to continue the proceedings in his presence would not be feasible" [F:may-where] [M-a]
        IF course EQUALS `s 650(2)(c) cause the accused to be removed and to be kept out of court during the trial of an issue as to whether the accused is unfit to stand trial` AND (NOT `the court is satisfied that failure to remove the accused during the trial of the issue of fitness might have an adverse effect on the mental condition of the accused`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where it is satisfied that failure to do so might have an adverse effect on the mental condition of the accused" [F:may-where] [M-a]
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:13081 | (3) An accused is entitled, after the close of the case for the prosecution, to make full answer and defence personally or by counsel.
@ref s 650(3) (src:13081-13081)
GIVEN `the case for the prosecution has closed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 650(3) the accused is entitled to make full answer and defence personally or by counsel` MEANS
    IF `the case for the prosecution has closed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An accused is entitled, after the close of the case for the prosecution, to make full answer and defence personally or by counsel" [F:entitled] [M-a]

§ `Sections 650.01 and 650.02 -- Designation of counsel of record; remote appearance`

-- src:13083 | 650.01 (1) An accused may appoint counsel to represent the accused for any proceedings under this Act by filing a designation with the court.
@ref s 650.01(1) (src:13083-13083)
GIVEN `the accused files a designation with the court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 650.01(1) the accused may appoint counsel to represent the accused for any proceedings under this Act` MEANS
    IF `the accused files a designation with the court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by filing a designation with the court"

-- src:13085 | (2) The designation must contain the name and address of the counsel and be signed by the accused and the designated counsel.
@ref s 650.01(2) (src:13085-13085)
GIVEN `the designation contains the name of the counsel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the designation contains the address of the counsel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the designation is signed by the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the designation is signed by the designated counsel` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 650.01(2) the designation has the contents subsection (2) requires` MEANS
    IF `the designation contains the name of the counsel` AND `the designation contains the address of the counsel` AND `the designation is signed by the accused` AND `the designation is signed by the designated counsel`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The designation must contain the name and address of the counsel and be signed by the accused and the designated counsel" [M-a] [F:duty]

-- src:13086 | Effect of designation
-- src:13087 | (3) If a designation is filed,
-- src:13088 | (a) the accused may appear by the designated counsel without being present for any part of the proceedings, other than
-- src:13089 | (i) a part during which oral evidence of a witness is taken,
-- src:13090 | (ii) a part during which jurors are being selected, and
-- src:13091 | (iii) an application for a writ of habeas corpus;
@ref s 650.01(3)(a) (src:13086-13091)
DECLARE `s 650.01(3)(a) the part of the proceedings` IS ONE OF
    `s 650.01(3)(a)(i) a part during which oral evidence of a witness is taken`
    `s 650.01(3)(a)(ii) a part during which jurors are being selected`
    `s 650.01(3)(a)(iii) an application for a writ of habeas corpus`
    `s 650.01(3)(a) some other part of the proceedings`

-- src:13086 | Effect of designation
-- src:13087 | (3) If a designation is filed,
-- src:13088 | (a) the accused may appear by the designated counsel without being present for any part of the proceedings, other than
-- src:13089 | (i) a part during which oral evidence of a witness is taken,
-- src:13090 | (ii) a part during which jurors are being selected, and
-- src:13091 | (iii) an application for a writ of habeas corpus;
@ref s 650.01(3)(a) (src:13086-13091)
GIVEN `a designation is filed` IS A BOOLEAN
      part IS A `s 650.01(3)(a) the part of the proceedings`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 650.01(3)(a) the accused may appear by the designated counsel without being present for the part` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a designation is filed` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a designation is filed" [F:may-if]
        IF part EQUALS `s 650.01(3)(a) some other part of the proceedings` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "without being present for any part of the proceedings, other than (i) a part during which oral evidence of a witness is taken, (ii) a part during which jurors are being selected, and (iii) an application for a writ of habeas corpus" [F:unless] [M-a]

-- src:13092 | (b) an appearance by the designated counsel is equivalent to the accused’s being present, unless the court orders otherwise; and
@ref s 650.01(3)(b) (src:13092-13092)
GIVEN `a designation is filed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court orders otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 650.01(3)(b) an appearance by the designated counsel is equivalent to the accused’s being present` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a designation is filed` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a designation is filed"
        IF `the court orders otherwise` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an appearance by the designated counsel is equivalent to the accused’s being present, unless the court orders otherwise" [F:unless] [M-a]
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:13093 | (c) a plea of guilty may be made, and a sentence may be pronounced, only if the accused is present, unless the court orders otherwise.
@ref s 650.01(3)(c) (src:13093-13093)
GIVEN `a designation is filed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused is present` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court orders otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 650.01(3)(c) a plea of guilty may be made and a sentence may be pronounced` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a designation is filed` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a designation is filed"
        IF `the accused is present` OR `the court orders otherwise` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a plea of guilty may be made, and a sentence may be pronounced, only if the accused is present, unless the court orders otherwise" [M-a]

-- src:13095 | (4) If the court orders the accused to be present otherwise than by appearance by the designated counsel, the court may
-- src:13096 | (a) issue a summons to compel the presence of the accused and order that it be served by leaving a copy at the address contained in the designation; or
-- src:13097 | (b) issue a warrant to compel the presence of the accused.
