DECLARE `s 650.01(4) the step` IS ONE OF
    `s 650.01(4)(a) issue a summons to compel the presence of the accused and order that it be served by leaving a copy at the address contained in the designation`
    `s 650.01(4)(b) issue a warrant to compel the presence of the accused`
    `s 650.01(4) some other step`

-- src:13095 | (4) If the court orders the accused to be present otherwise than by appearance by the designated counsel, the court may
-- src:13096 | (a) issue a summons to compel the presence of the accused and order that it be served by leaving a copy at the address contained in the designation; or
-- src:13097 | (b) issue a warrant to compel the presence of the accused.
@ref s 650.01(4) (src:13095-13097)
GIVEN `the court orders the accused to be present otherwise than by appearance by the designated counsel` IS A BOOLEAN
