`s 652(2) the failure to comply with the directions affects the validity of the proceedings` MEANS
    IF `the failure is a failure to comply with directions given under subsection 652(2)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "failure to comply with any directions given under this subsection does not affect the validity of the proceedings" [M-a]
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any directions given under this subsection"

